From d001d32ee269b34ade5924da34082af4b7f91be0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:44:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Use vkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties2KHR for placed
 memory map properties.

In WoW64 processes, init_physical_device() queries the placed memory map
properties of drivers with VK_EXT_map_memory_placed through the core
vkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties2. The instance win32u creates for D3DKMT
asks for no API version, so it is a Vulkan 1.0 instance where only the
KHR alias of that function exists, and Mesa drivers return NULL for the
core name. The call crashed inside D3DKMTOpenAdapterFromLuid, which left
the pthread_once of the D3DKMT instance unfinished; the next display
mode change then took the display lock and aborted on the recursive
once, leaving the lock held. 32-bit D3D9 games through DXVK hung when
they switched to full screen on KosmicKrisp.

The external memory host branch below already uses the KHR alias.
---
 dlls/win32u/vulkan.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
index 9497c6a69cc..de45d48c43e 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -1075,7 +1075,7 @@ static VkResult init_physical_device( struct vulkan_physical_device *physical_de
             VkPhysicalDeviceMapMemoryPlacedPropertiesEXT map_placed_props = {.sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_MAP_MEMORY_PLACED_PROPERTIES_EXT};
             VkPhysicalDeviceProperties2 props = {.sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_PROPERTIES_2,.pNext = &map_placed_props};
 
-            instance->p_vkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties2( host_physical_device, &props );
+            instance->p_vkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties2KHR( host_physical_device, &props );
             physical_device->map_placed_align = map_placed_props.minPlacedMemoryMapAlignment;
             TRACE( "Using placed map with alignment %u\n", physical_device->map_placed_align );
         }
